assistant
<think> Alright, so I have this problem here about a regular 15-sided polygon, also known as a pentadecagon, with each side length being 2a. The question is asking for the area of the annulus that's bounded by the circles inscribed in and circumscribed around this 15-sided polygon. Hmm, okay. Let me try to unpack this step by step. First off, I know that an annulus is the region between two concentric circles, right? So in this case, one circle is the inscribed circle (incircle) of the polygon, and the other is the circumscribed circle (circumcircle) that passes through all the vertices of the polygon. The area of the annulus would then be the area of the larger circle (the circumcircle) minus the area of the smaller circle (the incircle). Makes sense so far. 

